{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Project Owner Agent Configuration",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "description": "Create, complete configuration read and original create-command Lookup on an existing initialized Project. No Agent update/delete, AgentRun or Tool execution. Real Account cookie/Host/Origin/Fetch-Metadata and unsafe CSRF checks apply; administrators have no cross-Owner bypass. Creation requires the complete real Model/Tool/Mount/Secret/Skill initialization graph, including false defaults and empty arrays. All bodies and representations are bounded by 512 KiB; full Lookup uses the same cap to preserve legal 32 KiB instructions. Strict exact-key JSON rejects unknown/duplicate/case-alias keys, null outside nullable fields, invalid UTF-8/surrogates and trailing values. Byte caps (display 1024, description 8192, instructions 32768), Unicode controls/nonblank display, reserved names, sorted/combined references and cross-field relationships are validated by Go in addition to JSON Schema. No query, bare question mark or Content-Encoding on command routes. Native cancel/deadline/short-write/Close/Flush failure aborts and does not prove noncommit. Unknown retains the original key and intent. Runner declarations extend the same Agent command, with original authorization and atomic Agent/Mount/references/typed facts/receipt. They do not create physical directories or grant execution. Existing AgentConfig fields remain unchanged."
  },
